policy_module(hostpinger, 1.0.0)

# This module carries no rules. Everything it does is the file context in hostpinger.fc, which
# labels the launcher the way an ordinary service binary is labelled so that systemd transitions
# out of its own domain when it starts the unit.
#
# Without it the service runs as init_t — systemd's domain, entered by default because nothing
# under /usr/lib is an exec type any transition is defined for. init_t is granted neither the raw
# ICMP socket the service opens nor the exec of /usr/bin/ping that .NET falls back to, so the
# denials arrive as hosts that will not ping and a unit that will not stay up.
#
# bin_t is required rather than declared: it belongs to the base policy, and this module only
# hands out a label that already exists.
require {
	type bin_t;
}
